All four build_agent arms (anthropic, google, bedrock and OpenAI-compatible) now print the guessed-limits note; before, only google and the OpenAI-compatible arm did. It's committed as 4c29bbc6, and build, all tests (6985 passed), clippy and fmt are clean. I couldn't post the follow-up comment on #1021 because gh failed with HTTP 401: Bad credentials, so its last word is still the pre-fix comment.

Measured before wiring. The existing check needed no change:

| provider | id | result |
|---|---|---|
| anthropic | claude-opus-5-5 (default, and the model this loop runs on) | no note, because its preset declares real limits |
| anthropic | claude-made-up-9 (no preset) | note: 200000 / 16000 |
| bedrock | anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6 (the default) | note: 200000 / 16000 |
| bedrock | amazon.nova-pro-v1:0 | note: 200000 / 16000 |

Bedrock's default getting the note is correct: bedrock has no presets, so it really is running on a guess. I left the threshold alone; giving that default real limits is the next slice.

One change from the plan. The suggested real-binary check, --print-system-prompt, never builds the agent, so it prints no note for either id and can't tell them apart. The binary test (tests/guessed_limits_note_binary.rs) runs a real -p turn against a local stub instead. It checks that the stub's reply came back, that the preset id gets no note, and that the made-up id gets the exact line once.

Other tests:
• src/guessed_limits_arms_tests.rs has one row per case above with full-string expectations, plus a source check that counts 4 calls in build_agent.
• The existing call_site_is_not_quiet_gated test now expects 4 calls instead of 2.
• An older test comment that described the anthropic and bedrock gap now describes the current state.
• Removing the anthropic call (then restoring it in the same command) turned exactly the made-up-id binary test and the call-count check red, while the preset-id case stayed green.
• agent_builder.rs is at 4949 lines, under its cap of 4969, so tests/module_size.rs didn't need a new entry.

Docs: models.md now says anthropic ids without a preset and every bedrock id get the warning. The old "exactly two arms" sentence in ARCHITECTURE.md is kept and marked as superseded.

